components.design:
server.js's handleSeoPage() renders `<div id="app-embed" data-category="..."><script src="/app.js" type="module"></script>` on every SEO landing page, and serveStatic() falls back to /index.html (with `<div id="app">`) for the real app. app.js must detect which container is present and boot two different code paths. Sketch of public/index.html:

```html
<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
<title>buisnessfind — find great places near you</title>
<meta name="description" content="Search restaurants, cafes, groceries, gyms and more near your current location, with Google ratings and reviews.">
<script>
  // Anti-flash: runs before any CSS/paint. Must be inline, must not throw.
  (function () {
    try {
      var pref = localStorage.getItem('bf-theme') || 'system';
      var resolved = pref;
      if (pref === 'system' || !['aurora','midnight','meadow','sunset','mono'].includes(pref)) {
        resolved = window.matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches ? 'midnight' : 'aurora';
      }
      document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', resolved);
      document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme-pref', pref);
    } catch (e) {
      document.documentElement.setAttribute('data-theme', 'aurora');
    }
  })();
</script>
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/styles.css">
</head>
<body>
  <div id="app" class="app-shell" data-route="loading" aria-live="polite"></div>
  <noscript>buisnessfind needs JavaScript enabled to search and map nearby places.</noscript>
  <script type="module" src="/app.js"></script>
</body>
</html>
```

Note: `/api/geocode`, category chip icons etc. are NOT baked into this file — index.html stays a pure shell. `data-theme` is set synchronously by the inline script (reading localStorage), so styles.css never needs a `prefers-color-scheme` media query fallback for the app itself (only the inline boot script consults matchMedia, once, at load). app.js re-applies/watches theme after hydration (see component 2).

app.js entry / dual-mount detection:
```js
import { boot as bootApp } from './js/app-shell.js';
import { mount as mountEmbed } from './js/embed.js';

const full = document.getElementById('app');
const embed = document.getElementById('app-embed');
if (full) bootApp(full);
else if (embed) mountEmbed(embed, embed.dataset.category);
```
The embed path (used on every /restaurants-near-me-style SEO page) is deliberately lightweight: it fetches /api/config, geolocates, renders a mini map+list scoped to the one category baked into data-category, and shows a 'Open full app' link to `/#/map?category=<cat>` — no auth/friends chrome, so SEO pages stay fast and crawlable around it (the surrounding seo-copy/h1/faq from seo-content.js is server-rendered HTML the crawler sees regardless of JS).

